//! A unit: the bodies the emitter answered, closed under calls and placed as one translation unit
//! that says what it holds, so the runtime loads it without reading a source. The C it opens and
//! closes with is `compiler.emit.print.head`'s; the runtime it is compiled against describes what it
//! implements and lays out, and is refused where that disagrees with the compiler.

